    <!-- About / usage guide (AboutOverlay) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_Intro">StandbyAndTimer does three things to cut latency and stutter in games: it speeds up the Windows timer, clears the standby memory and gives your games priority. Closing the window keeps it running in the tray.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_TimerTitle">TIMER</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_Timer1">The Windows timer normally ticks about every 15.6 ms. Pressing TIMER brings that down to 0.5 ms, which makes frame pacing and input latency more consistent. The card shows the real value Windows reports.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_Timer2">The lock next to the TIMER title: UNLOCKED turns the timer on only when you press TIMER. LOCKED turns it on every time the app starts. IN GAME turns it on when a listed game starts and off when the last one exits. Each click moves to the next.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_Timer3">While the timer is on, Windows does not go to sleep by itself. With Settings → General → "Turn the timer off when idle", the timer goes off after the chosen time without input, so the PC can sleep; your next input turns it back on.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_Timer4">When the app closes, the timer goes back to the Windows default.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_StandbyTitle">STANDBY MEMORY</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_Standby1">Windows keeps files you used recently in RAM as "standby". That is normal and usually helps, but when free memory runs very low it can cause stutter in some games. "Clearable" is the current size of that list.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_Standby2">The Purge Standby button, the tray menu or the hotkey empties the list right away.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_Standby3">With AUTO PURGE on, the app checks every second: it purges when the list is above "List size at least" and free memory is below "Free memory lower than". If either value is 0, it never purges automatically.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_Standby4">"Only when idle": purges only after the given minutes without mouse or keyboard input. "Only while a game runs": purges only while a game from the Game Mode list runs. You can pick one of the two.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_Standby5">Light purge clears only the part Windows rates least likely to be used again. It is gentler but frees little on most systems.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_GameTitle">GAME MODE</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_Game1">With Game Mode on, a listed game that runs gets High priority and all CPU cores, and Windows' background throttling (EcoQoS) is switched off for it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_Game2">To add a game, press ADD or drag its .exe onto the list. The app also finds games running fullscreen and adds them with an AUTO tag; delete an AUTO game and it is never added again. Games are recognised by their .exe name.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_Game3">Select a game in the list and the two switches below apply to that game only. With "Give high priority" off the app leaves the game alone; turn it off if you use a tool such as Process Lasso (it applies the next time the game starts). With "Auto purge while it runs" off, automatic purges pause while that game runs.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_KeysTitle">HOTKEYS AND NOTIFICATIONS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_Keys1">Default hotkeys: Ctrl+Alt+P purges, Ctrl+Alt+T toggles the timer, Ctrl+Alt+O toggles auto purge. To change one, click it under Settings → Hotkeys and press the new keys; Esc cancels. Hotkeys work while the app is in the background.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_Keys2">Notifications appear on a purge, when the timer turns on or off, when a game is added to the list and when a listed game starts. Each one can be switched off under Settings → Notifications.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_MoreTitle">SETTINGS AND MORE</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_More1">Launch on startup: starts in the tray through Task Scheduler when you sign in to Windows.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_More2">Updates: the app looks for a new version on GitHub when it starts; download and install it from Settings. The download is checked with SHA256 and not installed if the check fails.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_More3">Export / Import Settings saves every setting and the game list to a file, to move them to another PC or keep a backup.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_More4">If something goes wrong: Settings → Open Log Folder. Uninstalling also removes the settings and the logs.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Help_More5">The app runs as administrator: the timer, the memory purge and game priority need it.</sys:String>

